; VSA90.INF - ViewSonic A90 (19" CRT) monitor description for Windows 9x.
;
; Windows 98 SE's in-box monitor database is dated April 1999 and stops short
; of this model: ViewSonic is present in MONITOR7.INF (43 entries) but the A90
; is not in any of the six stock INFs, so the Add New Hardware wizard asks for
; a driver on every boot and the display stays bound to "Default Monitor".
;
; A CRT "driver" is only a description: the model name, its horizontal and
; vertical sync ranges, and the largest mode it can take. Those ranges are
; what stop Windows offering a refresh rate the tube cannot display, so they
; are set conservatively for the A90 (30-95 kHz / 50-160 Hz, 1600x1200 max)
; rather than to the most optimistic figure in the brochure.
;
;
; NOT NEEDED ON .243 (checked 2026-08-13). That monitor reports a valid EDID,
; so Windows bound it itself as a Plug and Play Monitor:
;   Enum\Monitor\VSC504E\...  Driver=Monitor\0001  ConfigFlags=00000000
;   FriendlyName=A90  MonitorRanges=30-86,50-180,+,+  MaxResolution=1600,1200
; Those EDID ranges are BETTER than the conservative ones below, so installing
; this file there would be a downgrade. Keep it for a unit whose EDID is dead
; or whose cable has no DDC line, where Windows falls back to Default Monitor.
;
; The model lines carry the PnP hardware ID (Monitor\VSC504E, from the EDID's
; "VSC" vendor code plus product 504E). Without it Windows can only reach this
; INF through Have Disk - it can never match the detected monitor on its own,
; which is why an INF sitting in C:\WINDOWS\INF alone changes nothing.
;
; Install: Display Properties > Settings > Advanced > Monitor > Change >
;          Have Disk > C:\WINDOWS\INF\VSA90.INF

[Version]
Signature="$CHICAGO$"
Class=Monitor
ClassGUID={4D36E96E-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%MFG%

[Manufacturer]
%MFG%=ViewSonic

[ViewSonic]
%A90%=A90.Install,Monitor\VSC504E
%A90F%=A90.Install,Monitor\VSC504E

[A90.Install]
DelReg=Monitor.Del
AddReg=A90.AddReg, Monitor.Max, Monitor.DPMS

[Monitor.Del]
HKR,MODES
HKR,,MaxResolution
HKR,,DPMS

; "min-max horizontal kHz, min-max vertical Hz, sync polarities"
[A90.AddReg]
HKR,"MODES\1600,1200",Mode1,,"30.0-95.0,50.0-160.0,+,+"

[Monitor.Max]
HKR,,MaxResolution,,"1600,1200"

[Monitor.DPMS]
HKR,,DPMS,,1

[Strings]
MFG="ViewSonic"
A90="ViewSonic A90"
A90F="ViewSonic A90f"
